Manual review corrections, all local typographic defects rather than
upstream OpenStax mathematical content issues:

- The suitcase exercise's source MathML fused a whole "+width+" fragment
  (both plus signs and the word "width") into one <math> span alongside
  plain-prose "length"/"height", converting to
  `$+\text{width}+$` -- a Bin, Ord, Bin token sequence inside one formula.
  Per TeX's math-spacing rules the leading `+` (first atom in the group)
  demotes to Ord and gets no space before "width", while the trailing `+`
  (following an Ord) keeps its Bin spacing, producing visibly asymmetric
  "length +width + height" spacing. Split into three independent `$+$`
  spans (each a lone atom, so each demotes to Ord and carries no forced
  spacing of its own), relying on ordinary prose spacing between them:
  "length $+$ width $+$ height".
- The pizzeria intro sentence trapped a sentence-level semicolon plus
  manual `\,` spacing inside math (`$;\,a\,>\,c$`), continuing straight
  from prose "the number of pizzas". Moved the semicolon outside math and
  dropped the redundant manual spacing around `>` (already an automatic
  Rel-class gap): "the number of pizzas; $a>c$."
- The apartment-rent exercise trapped a sentence comma inside two
  `\text{month,}` spans (`$\$800/\text{month,}$`, `$\$25/\text{month,}$`),
  the same pattern as the related-rates review. Moved each comma outside
  its math span.

